   "location_summary": "Rodeo culture and bilingual communities give this Arkansas city a lively identity, set against the Ozark foothills.",
   "description": [
    {
     "title": null,
     "paras": [
      "Wake up at Villa Nica, named in honor of Nicaragua! There are two houses on the property—you’ll stay in the second house behind the front one. Perfect for groups, it offers 5 beds (2 fulls, 3 queens) for up to 10 guests. Just 4 minutes from downtown, 1 minute from the library, across from Springdale High School. Enjoy vaulted ceilings, ping pong, video games, and more.",
      "Did you know? 25% of proceeds from your booking go to Nicaraguan schools to help kids attend class and build a brighter future."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "The space",
     "paras": [
      "This newly built 2200 sqft home is perfect for large groups and families! With 5 comfortable beds (2 fulls, 3 queens), vaulted ceilings, and spacious living areas, everyone will have room to relax and unwind. The open-concept living room and dining areas are ideal for gatherings, movie nights, or game time.",
      "There are two houses on the property—you’ll stay in the second house behind the front one—so you get privacy while still enjoying the shared space. The property includes a large gravel parking lot with plenty of space for multiple vehicles."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Guest access",
     "paras": [
      "The property is self-check-in. The code to unlock the door will be shared with you 24 hours before your check-in time."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Other things to note",
     "paras": [
      "There is a spiral staircase that you need to go up to get to the beds. Baby gates are installed at bottom and top if needed. Also, ceilings are triangular in nature so be careful to not bump your head!"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "highlights": [
    {
